  "id": "split-stance-squat",
  "name": "Stationary Split Squat",
  "definition": "A stationary unilateral-emphasis compound exercise performed from a fixed sagittal split stance. The roster owns floor-supported barbell and paired-dumbbell split squats using an approximately leg-length stance, lead thigh-parallel endpoint, erect torso, full lead-foot contact, and rear-forefoot floor support. It also owns two source-exact rear-foot-elevated fixtures: a high-bar setup with the rear foot fixed at patella height and a two-dumbbell setup with the top of the rear foot supported on a bench of unreported height. Each keeps its contacts fixed and returns through lead-side hip extension, knee extension, and ankle plantarflexion. Dynamic lunges, unsupported rear-foot variants, other elevations, Smith, kettlebell, bodyweight, and deficit branches remain outside this contract.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "arnold-2010-lower-limb",
    "song-2023-split-squat-step-length",
    "stastny-2015-split-squat-dumbbell-position",
    "usmc-2017-dumbbell-split-squat",
    "nsca-2024-tsac-report-74-dumbbell-split-squat",
    "mackey-2021-bulgarian-split-squat",
    "nsca-2016-division-i-basketball-injury-screening"
  ],
